course: dictionary
lesson: 4058
title: Names with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names, and they start with a capital letter. A name can point to a place, a set of rules, or a person. «Switzerland has four national languages, German, French, Italian and Romansh; French is spoken in the west, around Geneva (Genève) and Lausanne.» Here Geneva is a place, because the sentence is about languages spoken around it.
explain: The same name can mean something else. «Henri Dunant helped start the Red Cross in 1863, and in 1864 countries signed the first Geneva Convention to protect wounded soldiers.» A convention is an agreement, so the Geneva Convention is a set of rules, not a city. Ask yourself: is this a place, a person, or a set of rules?
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like «around», «in» and «signed» tell you what kind of thing it is. If the sentence is about languages or maps, think place. If it is about war, fairness or agreements, think rules. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Geneva is a city in Switzerland, on Lake Geneva.
fact: Geneva is also a girl's name, and there are towns called Geneva in the USA.
fact: The Geneva Conventions are international rules about treating people fairly in war, including prisoners, the wounded and civilians.
fact: Many world organisations, such as parts of the United Nations and the Red Cross, have their headquarters in Geneva.
fact: Names always start with a capital letter, so Geneva always begins with a capital G.
exercise: In «French is spoken in the west, around Geneva», what does the word around tell you? | Geneva is a set of rules | Geneva is a type of food | * Geneva is a place that languages are spoken near | Geneva is a person's job
exercise: «The Geneva Conventions protect prisoners and the wounded in war.» What do the Geneva Conventions do? | Hold a famous fountain | * Set fair rules for treating people in war | Make new languages | Teach people to swim
exercise: «Henri Dunant helped start the Red Cross in 1863.» Which word in this sentence is a name? | 1863 | helped | start | * Dunant
test: In «Lake Geneva is beautiful», what is Geneva? | * A place | A rule about war | A word for sad | A brand of shoes
test: Why does Geneva start with a capital letter in «the first Geneva Convention»? | * It is part of a name | It is a question | It is at the start of a sentence | It is a colour
exam: A girl called Geneva says, «Geneva is my name.» What kind of name is it? | A type of weather | A school subject | A rule about war | * A girl's name
